# drivers/bluetooth/conf: Bluetooth.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver BT
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.bt.c
	help    the Bluetooth half of the WCN6750: step one, a read-only look at its three pins (bt=1)

driver BCM4361_BT
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.bcm4361_bt.c
	requires EXYNOS_HSI2C
	help    the Galaxy S9's Bluetooth, stage 1: the BCM4361's Bluetooth half on UART_BT, powered by BT_EN on the
	help    PCAL6524 expander, HCI over H4, and Broadcom's patch from the phone (bt=N there, 6 steps: 1 a look, 2 the
	help    expander, 3 the UART in loopback, 4 the chip powered, 5 HCI_Reset and its version, 6 the patch and the
	help    version again). No host stack. Needs the phone's bcm4361B2 .hcd in fw-bt/ for step 6 (BLUETOOTH.md of starlte)
